Grading by reading source only, no code execution.

**F1 Core loop** — `freshState()` builds one state object; `rngNext(rng)` (mulberry32-style) is the only randomness source (no `Math.random` calls found); `resolveTurn()` calls production→needs→morale→skill→crisis→hazard→trade→growth→endcheck in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map** — `generateGrid()` builds 8x8 via `rngWeighted(s.rng,...)`; `tryBuild()` checks `def.terrain.includes(t.terrain)`; `adjMult`/`hasAdjTerrain()` adds real amounts to ore/water/metal/power in `doProduction()`. Score 2.

**F3 Economy** — forge consumes ore+power→metal; greenhouse ash(implicit)→soil→(soil+water)→food; `addResource()` enforces `s.caps` and `logOverflow()` handles spillover. Score 2.

**F4 Population** — colonist records `{skill,fatigue,morale,job,assignedBuildingId}`; `skillFactor(c.skill)` and `computeMoraleFatigueFactor(c)` (reads fatigue+morale) both consumed in `doProduction()`. Score 2.

**F5 Needs** — `resolveNeeds()` consumes food/water per colonist, shortage calls `adjustAllMorale(s,-5)`; morale feeds `computeMoraleFatigueFactor` in production; `resolveMoraleFatigue()` allows morale recovery (not instant loss). Score 2.

**F6 Research** — 10 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `researchPrereqsMet()` gates `tryResearch()`; `payCost()` deducts; effects (`chainMult`,`condMult`,`mitigation`,unlock flags) read in `doProduction()`/`resolveHazard()`/`isBuildingUnlocked()`. Score 2.

**F7 Events** — 13 entries in `EVENTS`; `rngWeighted()` selection; 5 choice events (sickness, migrants, festival, wanderer, toxic_cloud) with distinct option effects; `eventCooldowns` set on fire and decremented every turn in `resolveHazard()`. Score 2.

**F8 Trade** — `resolveTrade()` prices use `stockRatio` (player stock/cap) and `market.drift[g]` (random-walked each caravan turn); `tradeBuy`/`tradeSell` both wired to UI and decrement/increment resources and caravan `qty`. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard** — `resolveHazard()` fires every 6 turns, severity scales with `s.turn`; but `doProduction()` only skips output when `b.disabled||b.hp<=0` — partial damage (hp>0) still produces at full rate, so "damaged buildings produce less" is binary not graduated; storm_walls/storm_shelter mitigate, `repairBuilding()` costs parts and restores. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load** — `serializeState()`→JSON into `#savearea` textarea; `deserializeState()` validates required fields/array shapes/rng shape and throws descriptive errors shown in `#loadmsg`. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions** — `checkEndConditions()` has reachable win (turn≥60, pop≥12, needs met) and lose (pop 0, or turn 60 without conditions) branches; `computeScore()` combines pop/research/turn/stockpile; `checkGameOverOverlay()` renders summary. Score 2.

**F12 UI** — `switchTab()` wired to nav buttons; log entries prefixed `[T'+e.turn+']`; `data-tip` tooltips explain resource/job/morale mechanics; keyboard Space + digits 1-5 wired in `init()`; `@media (max-width:500px)` adapts layout. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel** — `runTests()` has 18 assertions on real invariants (prereqs, save/load hash roundtrip, terrain rules, RNG determinism, clamps); `runBenchmark()` runs `greedyPolicyTurn()` headlessly for up to 200 turns and returns `hashState()`. Score 2.

**G1** — `efficient_chains`/`advanced_filtration` researchDone flags read as `chainMult`/`condMult` in `doProduction()`, applied to forge/greenhouse/condenser output every turn. Score 4.

**G2** — `resolveNeeds()` shortage → `adjustAllMorale(-5)` → `computeMoraleFatigueFactor(c)` multiplies output in `doProduction()`; fully wired each turn. Score 4.

**G3** — `resolveHazard()` damages `b.hp`; but `doProduction()` only zeroes output at `b.hp<=0` (disabled), partial damage produces at full rate; `repairBuilding()` restores hp/output for parts cost. Weak link matches rubric's "full rate until disabled" case. Score 1.

**G4** — `resolveTrade()` buy/sell prices computed from `stockRatio` and `market.drift[g]` (random-walked every caravan turn), read by `tradeBuy`/`tradeSell`. Score 4.

**G5** — sickness event: quarantine spends food/water+morale vs. ignore risks morale differently; migrants event: welcome calls `addColonist`+resource spend vs. turn-away grants scrip — real differing state mutations, not just log text. Score 4.

